    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207-a1">

                <pb facs="0433" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg377"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>No. 27.</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the In, Sho, Shi, Cho, Fu, and
                        Ken.</hi></p>
                <p>Hitherto the ichiroku (<hi rendition="#italic">i.e.</hi>, 1st, 6th, 11th, 16th,
                    21st, and 26th of each month) having been days of rest, proclamation is now made
                    that from next fourth month (April) Sunday has been fixed upon as the day of
                    rest. On Saturday there shall be rest from noon.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>SANJO SANEYOSKI.</item>
                            <item>DAIJO DAIJIN.</item>
                        </list></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="japanese-nengō"
                            when="1876-03-12">Twelfth of third month of ninth Meiji, (March 12,
                            1876.)</date></dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
